# GRACE & GRACE-FO Gravity Data Processing

Python pipeline for processing GRACE and GRACE-FO Level 2 satellite gravimetry data,
generating gravity anomaly maps, and analyzing temporal mass-change trends (e.g. ice
mass loss in Greenland/Antarctica) from spherical harmonic coefficients.

> **Note:** This repository is an independent rework of a data-processing pipeline
> originally developed with a 10-member team for a TU Delft research project on
> ice mass change assessment in Greenland. This version has been individually
> refactored and extended after the original project concluded.

## Overview

The pipeline covers three stages:

1. **Data** — reads raw/parsed GRACE and GRACE-FO Level 2 spherical harmonic
   coefficient data (2002 – Aug 2025).
2. **Gravity_Maps** — converts spherical harmonic coefficients into gravity
   values and renders single-date, double-date (comparative), and baseline
   heatmaps of Earth's gravity field.
3. **LSQR_Analysis** — applies signal filtering and weighted least-squares
   regression to estimate equivalent water height (EWH) / mass change over
   user-defined regions and time ranges.

